[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-31646"] :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-t,\\,2{t}^{2}-4t+2⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}-4t+2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-4t-1,4t-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨3(2)^{2}-4(2)-1,4(2)-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=2$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(2),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(2)| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-121717/selection/8979388da21670cd3070a6776f212b5c45d798469b729282bd5f47545984973a" :answer/id #uuid "42fa4738-f43d-5c85-b563-2e9ccede4609" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(2)=⟨\\frac{4}{3},3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121717/selection/bc83fd7721319223a974b8d45ca5ce240ae34fd1c244fb225212f136119a802a" :answer/id #uuid "32f50140-03af-5080-9774-aae2cd6586da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(2)=⟨\\frac{2}{3},2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121717/selection/65602e82cac46da550cb6d473d0f2593d0dce8b782c7476afd93097a079734b0" :answer/id #uuid "2b56afd4-dfbf-54fa-8b47-1951aaa8eee1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(2)=⟨\\frac{2}{3},3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121717/selection/601119bf001d9e7012b3e973af54b7d66a621e7fa3fcef39ceea29cfbf0833bc" :answer/id #uuid "62d988ce-7055-5dab-854b-dbfcf9561136" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(2)=⟨3,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121717/selection/a0fc969892e507d6f32e31ace3cd7513e02101ee5a2c61039d3a27744832315c" :answer/id #uuid "054f8b35-37f5-5d0b-a90a-573aaa235537" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(2)=⟨1,3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121717/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbe41e6f-133b-517c-85be-d9e88e35dd11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121717/selection/65602e82cac46da550cb6d473d0f2593d0dce8b782c7476afd93097a079734b0" :answer-field/choices ["q-121717/selection/8979388da21670cd3070a6776f212b5c45d798469b729282bd5f47545984973a" "q-121717/selection/bc83fd7721319223a974b8d45ca5ce240ae34fd1c244fb225212f136119a802a" "q-121717/selection/65602e82cac46da550cb6d473d0f2593d0dce8b782c7476afd93097a079734b0" "q-121717/selection/601119bf001d9e7012b3e973af54b7d66a621e7fa3fcef39ceea29cfbf0833bc" "q-121717/selection/a0fc969892e507d6f32e31ace3cd7513e02101ee5a2c61039d3a27744832315c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121717" :question/id #uuid "04e13fd6-9b6c-5320-b070-cd6f7b64eb13" :question/math-academy-id "q-121717" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\sqrt{4t+1},3t-2⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{4t+1}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4t+1}},3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2,$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4(2)+1}},3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9}},3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121717/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca363e2-c7b7-5196-bd38-10bcc30123ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121717"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121730/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :answer/id #uuid "12435079-d19e-5ffc-8ae6-38b74b4da42f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121730/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "566dc172-c0fd-5437-8058-aaa44298ad94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121730/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "e53547ec-5b80-57a7-891b-5a8b778e6b01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121730/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "16db51d7-5f3b-5f12-8b31-e7283fea8ee3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121730/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "54caf6ed-b72d-55b8-9639-eb529ca5484b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121730/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0962e7f-c716-569b-ac93-c27db645b4a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121730/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-121730/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" "q-121730/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-121730/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-121730/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-121730/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121730" :question/id #uuid "b9e2e9d7-7206-54bd-8133-c43a9871dfd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-121730" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=\\pi ,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\pi ) & =⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ⟩=⟨-4,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=\\pi $ we calculate the magnitude of $v(\\pi ),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(\\pi )| & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed when $t=\\pi $ is $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-121730/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "646467d1-f764-5a3c-b03b-7d74e588611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121730"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121739/selection/7161f3140020b0dd4c15ea58a14042b8788c2ceccaa922c051ca801a7112dea6" :answer/id #uuid "654fb3e3-066c-545e-bfb3-78caee10856f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121739/selection/24b44fba53578fd75922a19937c1240a9736e2dc7d7ad97ff6285932419cf4ea" :answer/id #uuid "605cd42b-68ff-5a62-baae-385cc923602a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121739/selection/8b5a8474a9b9934bc051275be5cb046d57f79f1810a453d2a6924c7b768a1f5e" :answer/id #uuid "b9caacc1-b6dc-5bf1-9d97-3ee15fe5da83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121739/selection/bddb16fb60275d07c2d2a20d0ff2251caf856d27ab8e69dbd10410685c39553a" :answer/id #uuid "75dda238-1f7d-5cf4-bd3c-e6e7fd3f6d6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121739/selection/95bc528a42f83cd4a53eb9e36d6b727f32c1b0eb864272fd8716dcc591ea8d15" :answer/id #uuid "fecc0fef-48e4-55e6-b47f-f2b91fd85fd1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The particle is never stationary" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121739/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf77831e-6e85-50c8-8e8a-fe8956f617d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121739/selection/bddb16fb60275d07c2d2a20d0ff2251caf856d27ab8e69dbd10410685c39553a" :answer-field/choices ["q-121739/selection/7161f3140020b0dd4c15ea58a14042b8788c2ceccaa922c051ca801a7112dea6" "q-121739/selection/24b44fba53578fd75922a19937c1240a9736e2dc7d7ad97ff6285932419cf4ea" "q-121739/selection/8b5a8474a9b9934bc051275be5cb046d57f79f1810a453d2a6924c7b768a1f5e" "q-121739/selection/bddb16fb60275d07c2d2a20d0ff2251caf856d27ab8e69dbd10410685c39553a" "q-121739/selection/95bc528a42f83cd4a53eb9e36d6b727f32c1b0eb864272fd8716dcc591ea8d15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121739" :question/id #uuid "e25e0179-be85-5825-a6d6-eefada53b4e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-121739" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{2}-6t,(t-3)^{5}⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-6t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-3)^{5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-6,5(t-3)^{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2(t-3),5(t-3)^{4}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨2(t-3),5(t-3)^{4}⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(t-3)=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=3, \\\\ 5(t-3)^{4}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=3$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121739/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11a24997-1f1e-5968-a331-980ca14be2f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121739"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352611/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "7c776a09-e4d0-5965-af20-3e036e3b0fb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352611/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "402cfa08-b520-55b1-9ae2-b86eff3f1e46" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352611/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-352611/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352611" :question/id #uuid "182941c7-4ee6-503e-a745-3ad3bae7e902" :question/math-academy-id "q-352611" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\frac{3(t-2)^{2}}{t+1},\\frac{3(t-2)^{2}}{t+5}⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary.\n\nThe particle is stationary at $t=$  \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3(t-2)^{2}}{t+1}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3(t-2)^{2}}{t+5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3(t-2)(t+4)}{(t+1)^{2}},\\frac{3(t-2)(t+12)}{(t+5)^{2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨\\frac{3(t-2)(t+4)}{(t+1)^{2}},\\frac{3(t-2)(t+12)}{(t+5)^{2}}⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(t-2)(t+4)}{(t+1)^{2}}=0\\, & ⇒\\,3(t-2)(t+4)=0\\,⇒\\,t=2,-4, \\\\ \\frac{3(t-2)(t+12)}{(t+5)^{2}}=0\\, & ⇒\\,3(t-2)(t+12)=0\\,⇒\\,t=2,-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=2$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352611/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11a24997-1f1e-5968-a331-980ca14be2f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352611"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
